set {flags.met_anna} = true
Anna Volkov, 9 AM. Work stress, insomnia. Referred by her GP.
She arrives three minutes early. You know this because she pointedly checks her watch when you open the door at the scheduled time.
Your desk is in a different configuration by the time you've both sat down.
"Sorry," Anna says, not sounding sorry at all. "Anyway."
- Let it go.
	She seems relieved you didn't mention it. You file it away for later.
	do PatientManager.add_trust("anna", 20)
- "You reorganized my desk."
	She goes briefly rigid. "It was just — the pen cup was on the left. That doesn't make sense."
	"Does it need to make sense?"
	A very long pause. "Anyway."
	do PatientManager.add_trust("anna", -5)
"The sleep thing," she says. "That's the main issue. I wake up at four and just — lie there. Thinking about what I didn't finish."
"What kind of things?"
- "Work tasks, you mean?" | [if {stats.knowledge} >= 2] [else="disable"] [alt_text="[Knowledge ≥ 2]"]
	"Yes. Mostly." A microsecond of hesitation. "Work things."
	You note the hesitation. She notes you noting it. A small negotiation passes between you.
	do PatientManager.add_trust("anna", 5)
	do GameState.add_stat_xp("knowledge", 1)
- "Is there a particular project weighing on you?"
	She blinks. "I — yes. There are several. I keep a log."
	She produces a color-coded notebook.
	do PatientManager.add_trust("anna", 5)
- "That sounds exhausting."
	"It is," she says, with evident relief that you're not asking follow-up questions.
	do PatientManager.add_trust("anna", 3)
"Your boss," she says eventually. "He gives me a lot of latitude. Which is obviously ideal."
"Obviously."
She doesn't look like it's ideal.
Before you can push further, she's already pivoting. "The desk — I could actually show you. A better layout."
"Please."
What follows is four minutes of silent, methodical rearrangement, conducted with the focused intensity of someone defusing a bomb she personally assembled.
[photo_opportunity id="anna_desk_demo" patient="anna" title="The Desk Demonstration" description="Anna reorganizes a stranger's workspace with surgical precision and audible satisfaction." portrait="res://assets/photos/anna/desk_demo.png"]
if {flags.last_photo_success}:
	Something in her expression as she steps back — a private, complete satisfaction — lands perfectly in the frame.
	do PatientManager.add_trust("anna", 3)
else:
	By the time you reach for your phone, she's already looking away. The moment dissolves.
She clears her throat. "Anyway. The sleep thing."
"Right," you say. "The sleep thing."
[add_note patient="anna" note="Presents with insomnia and work stress. Strong organizational compulsions — rearranged the office within two minutes of arrival."]
[add_note patient="anna" note="States boss gives her full autonomy. Her expression suggests this is not entirely welcome."]
do PatientManager.mark_session_done("anna")
jump between_patients/